<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav February inflation 0.6 pct vs 1.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav February inflation 0.6 pct vs 1.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INFLATION	   FEB	  JAN	 FEB 1996</p>
<p> monthly RPI index rise    + 0.6	+ 1.4	 + 4.8</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change	    +32.4	+37.7	+117.3</p>
<p>NOTES -- February RPI was up 16.5 percent against the average in 1996.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-February RPI was up 16.2 percent against the average in 1996 and 35 percent up against the same period last year.</p>
<p>Figures refer to rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro. -- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom ++381 11 222 4254</p>
